## Tiny-image cold-start check

To validate that rayon overhead doesn't bite at the smallest sizes,
synthetic 64×64 (1 group), 256×256 (1 group), 512×512 (4 groups)
PNGs were run on baseline 8T vs 1T. All sizes either no-op (sub-ms
xform on the 1-group cases) or win modestly at 4 groups
(512×512 e3: 1T ~4.8 ms, 8T ~3.7 ms = 1.30× speedup). Rayon's
`par_iter` over n=1 runs serially internally — no thread-wakeup cost
at the smallest sizes either.

## Reproducer

```bash
cd ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--w44-89-ac-chunking-guard

# Build BASELINE (no guard, baseline binary)
cargo build -p jxl-encoder-cli --release --features 'parallel butteraugli-loop'
cp target/release/cjxl-rs /tmp/cjxl-rs-baseline

# Apply guard via parallel_map_min, MIN_GROUPS_FOR_PARALLEL_XFORM=48
# (see git diff at commit 5232c16f or its parent)
cargo build -p jxl-encoder-cli --release --features 'parallel butteraugli-loop'
cp target/release/cjxl-rs /tmp/cjxl-rs-w44-89-guard

# Run interleaved A/B
for trial in 1 2 3 4 5; do
  for img in terminal codec_wiki imac_g3; do
    for eff in 3 4; do
      for thr in 1 8; do
        for build in baseline guard; do
          BIN=/tmp/cjxl-rs-${build}
          RAYON_NUM_THREADS=$thr __JXL_ENC_PHASE_TIMING=1 \
            $BIN ~/work/codec-corpus/gb82-sc/${img}.png \
            /tmp/out.jxl -d 1.0 -e $eff 2>&1 | grep 'encode_inner:'
        done
      done
    done
  done
done
```

## Conclusion

- Task as specified ("add small-image guard for parallel xform") is
  invalid in current measurements — there is no regression to fix.
- Default ship decision: **no source change at the call site**. The
  `parallel_map_min` helper was added to `parallel.rs` for future
  use; the existing `parallel_map` call in
  `vardct/transform.rs:1232` stays untouched (modulo a documentation
  comment recording this honest-stop).
- If a future investigation finds a real small-input regression in
  another hot loop, `parallel_map_min(n, min_n, f)` is ready to wire
  in with a single line.
- W44-88's bench methodology (3 non-interleaved trials with no
  cool-down) is the suspect; future small-image perf work should use
  paired interleaved measurements with at least 5 trials per cell.
